enchilada: MSS stage 10 (mss=10): join open/WPA2-PSK networks for wifid, in-kernel 4-way handshake, en0 data path (Wi-Fi round 7)

mss=10 = mss=9 plus joining when wifid sends APPLE80211 ASSOCIATE (592 bytes, HakiOS layout:
the passphrase as typed becomes the PMK here by PBKDF2-SHA1, or the 32-byte PMK as given; neither
is ever logged). The station follows ath10k + mac80211 on WCN3990 TLV firmware, ported from
topaz 0129/0130 and checked against Linux v6.12 mac.c, wmi-tlv.c, htt_tx.c and htt_rx.c: the
AP is taken from the scan table (strongest with that SSID, or the BSSID asked for); its RSN
element must offer CCMP pairwise and PSK AKM without MFP required (else refused); SCAN_CHAN_LIST
with its channel active (the beacon hint), STA powersave off, VDEV_START -> VDEV_START_RESP,
PEER_CREATE, open-system AUTH and ASSOC_REQ (SSID, rates, our RSN element) as host MLME frames
through WMI MGMT_TX_SEND with retries, PEER_ASSOC (legacy rates) and VDEV_UP; then the WPA2 4-way
handshake in this kernel (EAPOL-Key v2, PTK by PRF-SHA1, MIC/ANonce/replay checks, GTK KDE by RFC
3394 unwrap; message 4 in the clear and completed before VDEV_INSTALL_KEY pairwise CCMP + group
and PEER_SET_PARAM AUTHORIZE), group rekeys while joined, and teardown (VDEV_DOWN, PEER_DELETE,
VDEV_STOP) on failure, deauth, kickout or DISASSOCIATE. Crypto is libkern's SHA-1 and AES (BearSSL
in this kernel), checked once against the 802.11i and RFC 3394 vectors. en0's Ethernet frames go
out as native-wifi to-DS frames through HTT TX_FRM (the 0267 fragment bank, 50-byte prefetch, HTC
bypassed as ath10k_htt_tx_64 does, slots freed by TX_COMPL_IND); RX_IN_ORD MSDUs with a clean
rx_attention become Ethernet frames for ifnet_input (our own echoed multicast dropped). wifid
gets ASSOCIATE_RESULT (1 / 21 wrong key / 9 timeout / 2), APPLE80211_M_ASSOC_DONE, then
SSID/BSSID/LINK_CHANGED; configd gets KEV_DL_LINK_ON and IFM_ACTIVE; SSID, BSSID, CHANNEL, RSSI,
CURRENT_NETWORK, AUTH_TYPE and STATE (2 joining, 4 joined) are answered (HakiOS
hakios.apple80211.c / hakios.net.c, APSL 2.0). No periodic scans while joining or joined. DHCP
packets are noted in the log (first 8). mss<=9 behave as before (ASSOCIATE stays EOPNOTSUPP).

